(
  'Italy Visa Requirements 2026: Complete Application Guide',
  'blog/italy-visa-requirements-guide',
  '<h2>Italy Visa Requirements 2026</h2><p>Planning a trip to Italy? Whether you''re visiting the Colosseum in Rome, cruising the canals of Venice, or exploring the Tuscan countryside, understanding Italy''s visa requirements is essential for a smooth journey.</p><h2>Do You Need a Visa for Italy?</h2><p>Italy is part of the Schengen Area, which means citizens of many countries can visit for up to 90 days within a 180-day period without a visa. However, travelers from countries outside the visa-free list must apply for a Schengen visa through the Italian consulate.</p><h3>Visa-Free Countries</h3><p>Citizens of the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, Japan, South Korea, and most EU/EEA countries do not need a visa for short stays (up to 90 days).</p><h3>Countries Requiring a Visa</h3><p>Travelers from India, Pakistan, Bangladesh, Nigeria, Philippines, and many African and Asian nations must obtain a Schengen visa before traveling to Italy.</p><h2>How to Apply for an Italian Schengen Visa</h2><h3>Step 1: Determine Your Visa Type</h3><p>Italy offers several visa categories: Tourist (Type C), Business, Student, Work, and Transit visas. Most travelers will need a Type C short-stay tourist visa.</p><h3>Step 2: Gather Required Documents</h3><ul><li>Completed Schengen visa application form</li><li>Two recent passport-size photographs (35x45mm)</li><li>Valid passport with at least two blank pages</li><li>Travel medical insurance (minimum €30,000 coverage)</li><li>Proof of accommodation</li><li>Round-trip flight reservation</li><li>Proof of financial means (bank statements for last 3 months)</li><li>Cover letter explaining purpose of visit</li></ul><h3>Step 3: Book an Appointment</h3><p>Schedule an appointment at the Italian consulate or VFS Global in your country.</p><h3>Step 4: Attend the Interview</h3><p>Present your documents and provide biometric data if not done in the last 59 months.</p><h2>Processing Time and Fees</h2><p>Standard processing takes 15 calendar days, up to 45 days during busy periods. Fee: €80 for adults, €40 for children aged 6-12.</p><h2>Tips for a Successful Application</h2><ul><li>Apply 4-6 weeks before travel date</li><li>Ensure documents are in English or Italian</li><li>Show sufficient financial resources (€50-100 per day)</li><li>Have Schengen-specific travel insurance</li></ul>',
  'Complete guide to Italy visa requirements 2026. Schengen visa application, required documents, fees, processing times, and tips.',
  'Italy Visa Requirements 2026 | Complete Schengen Visa Guide',
  'Italy visa requirements in 2026. Step-by-step application guide, documents, fees, and processing times for Italian Schengen visa.',
  ARRAY['italy visa', 'italian visa requirements', 'schengen visa italy', 'italy tourist visa'],
  'scheduled',
