  'Spain Visa Guide 2026: Tourist & Work Visa Requirements',
  'blog/spain-visa-requirements-guide',
  '<h2>Spain Visa Guide 2026</h2><p>Spain attracts over 85 million visitors annually. Understanding visa requirements is your first step to planning a Spanish adventure.</p><h2>Visa Requirements for Spain</h2><p>As a Schengen member, Spain follows the common visa policy for short stays. Citizens of over 60 countries can visit visa-free for up to 90 days.</p><h3>Who Needs a Visa?</h3><p>Passport holders from India, China, Nigeria, Pakistan, or Egypt need a Schengen visa through the Spanish consulate.</p><h2>Types of Spanish Visas</h2><ul><li><strong>Tourist Visa (Type C):</strong> For tourism or visiting family</li><li><strong>Business Visa:</strong> For meetings or conferences</li><li><strong>Student Visa (Type D):</strong> For programs longer than 90 days</li><li><strong>Work Visa:</strong> Requires a job offer from a Spanish employer</li><li><strong>Golden Visa:</strong> For investors (minimum €500,000 in real estate)</li></ul><h2>Required Documents</h2><ul><li>Completed application form</li><li>Valid passport (3+ months validity)</li><li>Two passport photos</li><li>Travel insurance (€30,000 minimum)</li><li>Proof of accommodation and flights</li><li>Bank statements</li></ul><h2>Fees</h2><p>Adults: €80, Children (6-12): €40, Under 6: Free.</p><h2>Spain Golden Visa</h2><p>Invest €500,000+ in real estate for residence rights and Schengen travel.</p>',
  'Spain visa guide 2026. Tourist, work, and Golden Visa requirements, documents, fees, and application process.',
  'Spain Visa Guide 2026 | Tourist & Work Visa Requirements',
  'Spain visa requirements 2026. Tourist visa, work visa, Golden Visa, documents, fees and application process.',
