  'ETIAS 2026: Europe''s New Travel Authorization System Explained',
  'blog/etias-europe-travel-authorization-2026',
  '<h2>ETIAS 2026</h2><p>ETIAS is the EU''s new electronic travel authorization for visa-exempt travelers visiting the Schengen Area. It is NOT a visa — it''s a pre-travel screening system similar to the US ESTA.</p><h2>Who Needs ETIAS?</h2><p>Citizens of ~60 visa-free countries including US, UK, Canada, Australia, Japan, and Brazil.</p><h2>How to Apply</h2><ol><li>Visit the official ETIAS website</li><li>Fill out the form (~10 minutes)</li><li>Pay €7 (free for under 18 or over 70)</li><li>Receive approval (usually within minutes)</li></ol><h2>Key Details</h2><ul><li>Validity: 3 years or until passport expires</li><li>Stay: Up to 90 days per 180-day period</li><li>Cost: €7</li><li>Covers: All 27 Schengen states plus Iceland, Liechtenstein, Norway</li></ul><h2>ETIAS vs. Schengen Visa</h2><p>ETIAS is simpler — no embassy visit, no documents, no interview. Quick online process for visa-exempt nationals only.</p>',
  'Guide to ETIAS - Europe''s new travel authorization launching in 2026. Who needs it, how to apply, costs, and key details.',
  'ETIAS 2026 | Europe Travel Authorization System Guide',
  'ETIAS 2026 guide. Who needs it, how to apply, fees, validity, and how it differs from a Schengen visa.',
